  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "A museum’s attendance decreased to $80%$ of its previous level. Then, a promotion increased attendance by $25%.$ If the museum originally had $24,000$ attendees, how many attendees were added by the promotion?\n\nThe number of attendees added is  \n{{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "First, the new attendance is $80%$ of the previous level $(24,000$ attendees$):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}80%\\times 24,000 & =\\frac{80}{100}\\times 24,000 \\\\  & =0.8\\times 24,000 \\\\  & =19,200\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the new attendance is $19,200.$ Then, the attendees added by the promotion is $25%$ of this new attendance:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25%\\times 19,200 & =\\frac{25}{100}\\times 19,200 \\\\  & =0.25\\times 19,200 \\\\  & =4,800\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the number of attendees added is $4,800.$",
